## Deployment

Deployed to AWS Lambda (Function URL, no API Gateway/ALB) behind the
[`lambda-web-app`](https://github.com/NateDogg12501/terraform-modules/tree/main/modules/lambda-web-app)
Terraform module{% if needs_datastore %}, with data in DynamoDB via
[`dynamodb-single-table`](https://github.com/NateDogg12501/terraform-modules/tree/main/modules/dynamodb-single-table){% endif %},
and Terraform state in S3 via
[`s3-bucket`](https://github.com/NateDogg12501/terraform-modules/tree/main/modules/s3-bucket).
Stays inside AWS Always Free.

```bash
cd terraform/bootstrap    # once per project: creates the S3 state bucket
terraform init && terraform apply

cd .. && terraform init   # against that bucket
terraform apply
```

The first two lines are once per project, not once per deploy — after that,
deploying is `terraform apply` in `terraform/`. See `terraform/README.md` for the
SSM parameters needed before the first apply, and for what to do if `terraform
init` says `NoSuchBucket`.
{% else -%}
## Deployment

None — this project is local-only by design (the HOSTED capability was off
when it was scaffolded). If that changes, set `needs_hosting: true` in
`.copier-answers.yml` and run `copier update`{% if not needs_api %} — HOSTED deploys a Node
handler, so `needs_api` has to go on at the same time{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
